1. Overview

This data mapping document defines the field-level migration of member demographic, enrollment, PCP history, communication preference, and address data from the Enterprise Data Hub (EDH) source system to Microsoft Dataverse CRM, as specified by the provided DDLs and business requirements. The mapping ensures data consistency, format standardization (E.164 for phone, ISO 8601 for dates, RFC 5322 for emails), and strict data type alignment between source and target schemas. Key considerations include enforcement of referential integrity, mandatory field population, deduplication of Member IDs, and compliance with PHI access and auditability constraints. All transformation rules are grounded in the actual DDLs, sample data, and explicit constraints, with no omissions or assumptions. Constraints such as mandatory fields, uniqueness, format validation, and audit logging directly shape mapping logic and are strictly enforced.

